<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia May palm oil exports 672,805t-SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia May palm oil exports 672,805t-SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said on Monday it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for May at 672,805 tonnes against 641,520 tonnes for April.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 223,761 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 264,519 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 53,989 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products totalled 130,536 tonnes.  </p>
<p>Pakistan the top buyer during the period, taking 148,090 tonnes, followed by India which bought 130,706 tonnes, China (85,600 tonnes) and Japan (39,400 tonnes).</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 65,180 tonnes. -- Tan Lee Lee - Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
